<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>org.GraphDefined.Vanaheimr.XMPPConsole</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Only the log of the output any more: the console writes itself and needs
      a logger for that. BouncyCastle stood here as long as OMEMO lay here -
      since D97 it does not any more, and a package nobody uses is a claim
      about a dependency that does not exist.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging" Version="10.0.10" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Console" Version="10.0.9" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      A sibling directory, not a submodule under libs/. This repository used to
      pin its own Hermod, Styx and Ratatoskr, which made it the one build in
      the family that could not drift - and the one that could not be built
      *with* anything. Its Ratatoskr was a different revision from the one
      XMPPConformanceTests pins, so a tree holding both held two, and no
      solution could contain the console and the conformance suite at once
      without two Ratatoskr.csproj producing the same assembly.

      Now it reaches sideways like everything else does: Ratatoskr reaches for
      ..\..\Hermod, Hermod for ..\..\Styx, and this for ..\..\Ratatoskr. The
      layout that satisfies all three is the four checked out beside each
      other:

          XMPPConsole/   Ratatoskr/   Hermod/   Styx/

      and inside XMPPConformanceTests that layout already exists under libs/,
      where this resolves to the Ratatoskr that repository pins.

      What it costs is named rather than hidden: this project now builds
      against whatever Ratatoskr sits beside it, so a breaking change over
      there turns it red without anything here having moved. That is the same
      bargain Hermod, Styx and Ratatoskr have always made, and the reproducible
      build lives in the one place that pins all four.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Ratatoskr\Ratatoskr\Ratatoskr.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
